Done in efe50dfa3 — `hidden_states_quant.py` is renamed to `quant.py` (git-tracked rename; `moe_methods.py` was its only importer), and `HiddenStatesDynamicQuant` now routes by dtype:

```python
def __init__(self, quant_dtype: torch.dtype) -> None:
    super().__init__(quant_dtype)
    if quant_dtype == torch.float8_e4m3fn:
        self._op = torch.ops.npu.npu_dynamic_mx_quant
    elif quant_dtype in (torch.int8, torch.quint4x2):
        self._op = torch.ops.npu.npu_dynamic_quant
    else:
        raise ValueError(f"Unsupported dynamic quant dtype: {quant_dtype}")
```

The two existing call sites use `quint4x2` and `int8`, so this commit is behaviour-preserving; the `float8_e4m3fn` branch has no consumer yet — it gets wired up as the DeepEP fallback in the other thread.

I wrote it fresh rather than cherry-picking from #29762 for one reason: that version does a module-level `import torch_npu`, which breaks the CUDA/CPU/AMD/XPU CI jobs (the module is imported on every platform). Going through `torch.ops.npu.*` keeps it importable everywhere, and `torch.float8_e4m3fn` is a plain torch dtype so no `torch_npu` reference is needed here at all. If `float4_e2m1fn_x2` is added later it will need the lazy `getattr(torch_npu, ...)` treatment, as in `_get_float4_e2m1fn_x2_dtype()`.

Done in 2d06d61a5 — `GroupedMatmulSwigluQuant` now lives in `npu/moe/matmul.py` next to `GroupedMatmul`, same `**scale_args` passthrough style.

Three things to know if another scheme picks it up:

- it returns `(quantized_activations, block_scale)` rather than a single tensor, because the requant is part of the kernel;
- it takes no `output_dtype` — the output dtype comes from `quant_dtype` in `scale_args`;
- the count → cumulative `group_list` conversion moved inside the wrapper, since this op wants cumulative while `npu_grouped_matmul` keeps the count form the dispatcher produces. That asymmetry is now documented in one place instead of being open-coded at the call site.

The resulting op call is argument-for-argument identical to the previous one, and online + offline are re-validated on A5.
